   "old": "\n\n<figcaption>Two pairs of molecules are shown where each molecule has one larger blue side labeled &ldquo;delta sign, negative sign&rdquo; and a smaller red side labeled &ldquo;delta sign, positive sign. In the first pair, the red sides of the two molecules both face to the left and the blue side to the right. A horizontal dotted line lies in between the two. In the second pair, the molecules face up and down, with the red and blue ends aligning. A horizontal dotted line lies between the red and blue ends facing upward and another lies between the red and blue ends facing downward.</figcaption>",
   "new": "",
   "count": 1,
   "note": "1.8 Fig 7 second caption (old alt)"
  },
  {
   "old": "\n\n<figcaption>Five water molecules are shown near one another, but not touching. A dotted line lies between many of the hydrogen atoms on one molecule and the oxygen atom on another molecule.</figcaption>",
   "new": "",
   "count": 1,
   "note": "1.8 Fig 8 second caption (old alt)"
  },
  {
   "old": "\n\n<figcaption>Three figures are shown. The first is a photo of the bottom of a gecko&rsquo;s foot. The second is bigger version which shows the setae. The third is a bigger version of the setae and shows the spatulae.</figcaption>",
