   "note": "597054 caption was old alt text"
  },
  {
   "old": "<figcaption>Cl with 7 dots surrounding it plus Cl with 7 dots surrounding it means they are chlorine atoms. To turn into a chlorine molecule, have two dots in between each Cl and 6 dots surrounding each Cl on the sides that aren't connected. (Figure from <em>The Basics of General, Organic, and Biological Chemistry</em> by Ball, Hill and Scott, CC BY-NC-SA 3.0.)</figcaption>",
   "new": "<figcaption>Two chlorine atoms, each with seven valence electrons, share one pair to form Cl<sub>2</sub>. (Figure from <em>The Basics of General, Organic, and Biological Chemistry</em> by Ball, Hill and Scott, CC BY-NC-SA 3.0.)</figcaption>",
   "count": 1,
   "note": "597054 caption was old alt text"
  },
